  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "attrs": {
      "localId": "042720aac3bc"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "If a resource is both deleted and its tombstone cleaned up in the same fedora transaction, then containment table entries related to the purged resource are not cleaned up. This blocks purging of tombstones of any ancestors of the object. I am able to replicate the issue with the following commands:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "language": "shell",
      "localId": "c58c174a-a1ab-469d-a9bf-1cb7ebc460ca",
      "wrap": true
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "curl -XPUT http://localhost:8088/rest/my -ufedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin -v\ncurl -XPUT http://localhost:8088/rest/my/path -ufedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin\nTXLOCATION=$(curl -s -ufedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin -D - -X POST \"http://localhost:8088/rest/fcr:tx\" -o /dev/null | grep -i '^Location:' | awk '{print $2}' | tr -d '\\r')\ncurl -XDELETE http://localhost:8088/rest/my/path -ufedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin -v -H \"Atomic-ID: $TXLOCATION\"\ncurl -XDELETE http://localhost:8088/rest/my/path/fcr:tombstone -ufedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin -v  -H \"Atomic-ID: $TXLOCATION\"\ncurl -ufedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin -XPUT \"$TXLOCATION\"\ncurl -XDELETE http://localhost:8088/rest/my -ufedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin -v\ncurl -XDELETE http://localhost:8088/rest/my/fcr:tombstone -ufedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin -v",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "codeBlock"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "localId": "07aa315da2c6"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "All of the commands succeed except for the last one, which fails with 04 ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "code"
        }
       ],
       "text": "Error: Resource /my/path not found",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": ". If you look in the containment table afterwards, there are still entries for both ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "code"
        }
       ],
       "text": "/my/path",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " and ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "code"
        }
       ],
       "text": "/my",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": ", with end dates indicating that they were soft deleted but not purged. However, the OCFL object for ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "code"
        }
       ],
       "text": "/my/path",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " is gone at this point.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
